4. Authorized Individuals and Exceptions

4.1. Authorized Individuals

The right to modify and distribute the Software before its official release is exclusively granted to individuals personally authorized by the repository owner.
Authorized individuals are those whom the repository owner has personally and explicitly added to the list of contributors in the **Development Contributors** section of the `LEGAL.md` file in the project's official GitHub repository.
Merely having access to the source code, being able to view the repository, download files, or create forks does not grant any such rights.

4.2. Limitations of Authorization

Granted permissions are strictly limited to the scope of authorization established by the repository owner.
Authorized individuals may not transfer their permissions to third parties, grant them permission to modify or distribute the Software, or issue sublicenses of their own.
Removing an individual from the contributors list of the official repository terminates their authorization to further modify and distribute the Software, unless otherwise separately agreed upon with the copyright holder.

4.3. Individual Permissions

The copyright holder may grant additional permissions to specific individuals or legal entities in writing.
Permission granted to one individual or entity does not automatically extend to any other individuals or entities.

